    """The item at the end of the edge."""
    node: Voucher!

    """A cursor for use in pagination (the row's keyset sort key)."""
    cursor: String!
}

# Saleor's promotion where-filter input — the declared wire shape of
# the where argument (see promotions: an explicit classified error
# until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids
# carries the scalar filter surface; name (its StringFilterInput
# closure), startDate/endDate (DateTimeFilterInput), isOldSale, type
# (PromotionTypeEnumFilterInput), metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
# closure) and the AND/OR combinators stay undeclared until an owning
# capability exists — any where use answers the classified
# not-implemented error before field-level semantics matter, and a
# Dashboard query naming an undeclared sub-field fails schema
# validation loudly (never a silent no-op).
input PromotionWhereInput {
    ids: [ID!]
}

# Saleor's voucher filter input — the declared wire shape of the
# filter argument (see vouchers: an explicit classified error until
# the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: search/ids
# carry the scalar filter surface; status (DiscountStatusEnum list),
# timesUsed (IntRangeInput), discountType (VoucherDiscountType list),
# started (DateTimeRangeInput) and metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
# closure) stay undeclared until an owning capability exists — the
# same declared-shape rule the StaffUserInput/ProductTypeFilterInput
# precedents established.
input VoucherFilterInput {
    search: String
    ids: [ID!]
}

# Saleor's promotion sorting input and field vocabulary — the full
# pinned enum is declared verbatim; NAME and CREATED_AT execute as
# the real forward-only keyset sorts (the owning non-null columns,
# id tiebreaker); START_DATE/END_DATE (the optional policy-window
# columns) answer the explicit not-implemented error. direction
# reuses the EXISTING shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
input PromotionSortingInput {
    """Specifies the direction in which to sort promotions."""
    direction: OrderDirection!

    """Sort promotions by the selected field."""
    field: PromotionSortField!
}

enum PromotionSortField {
    """Sort promotions by name."""
    NAME

    """Sort promotions by start date."""
    START_DATE

    """Sort promotions by end date."""
    END_DATE

    """Sort promotions by creation date."""
    CREATED_AT
}

# Saleor's promotion type vocabulary — declared verbatim; ORDER is the
# owning fact (every platform promotion is an order-level policy),
# CATALOGUE stays inert SDL vocabulary (never emitted by this
# platform).
enum PromotionTypeEnum {
    CATALOGUE
    ORDER
}

# Saleor's discount value type vocabulary — declared verbatim; the
# owner's PERCENTAGE/FIXED row vocabulary renders through it exactly.
enum DiscountValueTypeEnum {
    FIXED
    PERCENTAGE
}

# Saleor's voucher sorting input and field vocabulary — the full
# pinned enum is declared verbatim (CODE deprecated upstream with no
# reason string in the pinned schema); CODE executes as the real
# forward-only keyset sort (the row's non-null normalized code, id
# tiebreaker); NAME/START_DATE/END_DATE (optional columns),
# VALUE/MINIMUM_SPENT_AMOUNT (channel-scoped money upstream + the
# frozen money contract), TYPE (no voucher-type discrimination) and
# USAGE_LIMIT (optional column) answer the explicit not-implemented
# error, as does the deprecated nested channel. direction reuses the
# EXISTING shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
input VoucherSortingInput {
    """Specifies the direction in which to sort vouchers."""
    direction: OrderDirection!

    """Specifies the channel in which to sort the data."""
    channel: String @deprecated(reason: "Use root-level channel argument instead.")

    """Sort vouchers by the selected field."""
    field: VoucherSortField!
}

enum VoucherSortField {
    """Sort vouchers by code."""
    CODE @deprecated

    """
    Sort vouchers by name.

    Added in Saleor 3.18.
    """
    NAME

    """Sort vouchers by start date."""
    START_DATE

    """Sort vouchers by end date."""
    END_DATE

    """
    Sort vouchers by value.

    This option requires a channel filter to work as the values can vary between channels.
    """
    VALUE

    """Sort vouchers by type."""
    TYPE

    """Sort vouchers by usage limit."""
    USAGE_LIMIT

    """
    Sort vouchers by minimum spent amount.

    This option requires a channel filter to work as the values can vary between channels.
    """
    MINIMUM_SPENT_AMOUNT
}


# === Campaign packet campaign-b5-a: the Saleor product-variant wire types ===
# "Represents a version of a product such as different size or color." —
# the BOUNDED closure over the catalog owner's product_variants row: id
# (the typed global ID), name (the variant's own optional display column —
# NULLABLE on the wire because the row's own column carries no
# non-null constraint; the registered nullable-name divergence from
# upstream's non-null name), sku (the seller's own SKU — non-null on
# this platform, nullable upstream stays compatible), product (the
# parent's bounded projection through the EXISTING Product wire type —
# one Product shape across the product roots and the variant roots),
# and status (a PLATFORM EXTENSION fact: the variant's own
# ACTIVE/SUSPENDED/ARCHIVED availability lifecycle). Unowned Saleor
# fields (the metadata family, the channel-scoped pricing/
# channelListings family, weight, the attribute selections,
# quantityOrdered/revenue reporting, media, translations, updatedAt,
# trackInventory, quantityLimitPerCustomer, preorder facts) stay
# undeclared until an owning capability exists — never faked.
type ProductVariant {
    """The ID of the product variant — typed global ID (opaque, never a raw UUID)."""
    id: ID!

    """Name of the product variant (the entity's own optional display column — the honest null of a legacy free-form variant)."""
    name: String

    """The seller's own SKU (non-null on this platform)."""
    sku: String

    """The product to which the variant belongs (the parent's bounded projection — the SAME Product wire type the product roots serve)."""
    product: Product!

    """The variant's availability lifecycle (a platform extension fact: ACTIVE/SUSPENDED/ARCHIVED)."""
    status: String!
}

# Saleor's connection envelope for countable product-variant lists —
# declared (not runtime-generated) so the exact Saleor shape stands,
# including totalCount. Spring's ConnectionTypeDefinitionConfigurer
# skips already-declared connection types (the measured
# declared-types-skip behavior the ProductCountableConnection
# declaration recorded), so this declaration wins and the generated
# connections elsewhere are untouched. pageInfo reuses the EXISTING
# shared PageInfo type — not redeclared.
type ProductVariantCountableConnection {
    """Pagination data for this connection."""
    pageInfo: PageInfo!

    edges: [ProductVariantCountableEdge!]!

    """A total count of items in the collection (the caller-scope population's own count)."""
    totalCount: Int
}

# Saleor's edge for the countable product-variant connection — the
# node/cursor pair the keyset scroll emits (per-element opaque cursors
# over the executed sort's own keys).
type ProductVariantCountableEdge {
    """The item at the end of the edge."""
    node: ProductVariant!

    """A cursor for use in pagination."""
    cursor: String!
}

# Saleor's product-variant filter input — the declared wire shape of the
# filter argument (see productVariants: an explicit classified error
# until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: search and
# sku carry the scalar filter surface; metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
# closure), isPreorder (the deprecated preorder fact) and updatedAt
# (DateTimeRangeInput) stay undeclared until an owning capability exists
# — the same declared-shape rule the ProductTypeFilterInput precedents
# established.
input ProductVariantFilterInput {
    search: String
    sku: [String!]
}

# Saleor's product-variant where input — the declared wire shape of the
# where argument (see productVariants: an explicit classified error
# until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids
# carries the scalar filter surface; sku (its StringFilterInput closure),
# updatedAt (DateTimeRangeInput), metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
# closure), attributes (the AssignedAttributeWhereInput family) and the
# AND/OR combinators stay undeclared until an owning capability exists —
# any where use answers the classified not-implemented error before
# field-level semantics matter, and a Dashboard query naming an
# undeclared sub-field fails schema validation loudly (never a silent
# no-op).
input ProductVariantWhereInput {
    ids: [ID!]
}

# Saleor's product-variant sorting input — the full pinned vocabulary
# (upstream's own two values, verbatim): BOTH fields execute as the real
# forward-only keyset sorts (LAST_MODIFIED_AT over the entity's own
# non-null updated_at audit column, ID over the unique key), in both
# directions, deterministic with the id tiebreaker where the sort field
# is not already unique. direction reuses the EXISTING shared
# OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
input ProductVariantSortingInput {
    """Specifies the direction in which to sort productVariants."""
    direction: OrderDirection!

    """Sort productVariants by the selected field."""
    field: ProductVariantSortField!
}

enum ProductVariantSortField {
    """Sort product variants by last modification date."""
    LAST_MODIFIED_AT

    """
    Sort product variants by ID.

    Added in Saleor 3.23.
    """
    ID
}

# === Campaign packet campaign-b5-b: the Saleor order wire types ===
# "Represents a fulfillment order." — the BOUNDED closure over the
# orders owner's own rows: id (the typed global ID), created (the
# placement instant as the ISO-8601 string the house's deliberate
# no-new-scalar decision carries on the whole surface — the locked
# Boot 4.1.1 -> spring-graphql 2.0.5 -> graphql-java 25.0 chain adds
# no temporal scalar; the registered divergence from upstream's
# DateTime scalar), and status (the platform machine's own lifecycle
# rendered through Saleor's OrderStatus vocabulary by the registered
# ADAPT mapping: PLACED renders UNCONFIRMED, CONFIRMED renders
# UNFULFILLED, FULFILLED and CANCELLED render their upstream
# spellings; the other five upstream values stay inert SDL vocabulary
# this platform never emits). Unowned Saleor fields (the metadata
# family, number — no human-readable order-number column, user — the
# identity projection lands with the buyer-surface slice, the
# channel-scoped money/tax totals — money stays off the wire per the
# frozen money contract, billing/shipping addresses — no address
# store, the D-ADDR-001 decision, lines/fulfillments/deliveries,
# trackingClientId, languageCode, externalReference, updatedAt,
# events, discounts, payments, giftCards, invoices) stay undeclared
# until an owning capability exists — never faked.
type Order {
    """The ID of the order — typed global ID (opaque, never a raw UUID)."""
    id: ID!

    """Date and time when the order was created (the placement instant, ISO-8601 string — the no-new-scalar house decision)."""
    created: String!

    """Status of the order (the platform lifecycle rendered through Saleor's own vocabulary)."""
    status: OrderStatus!
}

# Saleor's connection envelope for countable order lists — declared
# (not runtime-generated) so the exact Saleor shape stands, including
# totalCount. Spring's ConnectionTypeDefinitionConfigurer skips
# already-declared connection types (the measured declared-types-skip
# behavior the ProductCountableConnection declaration recorded), so
# this declaration wins and the generated connections elsewhere are
# untouched. pageInfo reuses the EXISTING shared PageInfo type — not
# redeclared.
type OrderCountableConnection {
    """Pagination data for this connection."""
    pageInfo: PageInfo!

    edges: [OrderCountableEdge!]!

    """A total count of items in the collection (the whole live order population's own count)."""
    totalCount: Int
}

# Saleor's edge for the countable order connection — the node/cursor
# pair the keyset scroll emits (per-element opaque cursors over the
# executed sort's own keys).
type OrderCountableEdge {
    """The item at the end of the edge."""
    node: Order!

    """A cursor for use in pagination."""
    cursor: String!
}

# Saleor's order filter input — the declared wire shape of the filter
# argument (see orders: an explicit classified error until the owning
# query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: search and ids carry the
# scalar filter surface; status (OrderStatusFilter list),
# paymentStatus/authorizeStatus/chargeStatus (the deprecated legacy
# payments family), customer, created (DateRangeInput),
# channels/checkoutTokens/checkoutIds (the channel model the platform
# does not own), updatedAt (DateTimeRangeInput), isClickAndCollect,
# isPreorder, giftCardUsed/giftCardBought, numbers, metadata (its
# heavy MetadataFilter closure) stay undeclared until an owning
# capability exists — the same declared-shape rule the
# ProductTypeFilterInput precedents established.
input OrderFilterInput {
    search: String
    ids: [ID!]
}

# Saleor's order where input — the declared wire shape of the where
# argument (see orders: an explicit classified error until the owning
# query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids carries the scalar
# filter surface; everything else stays undeclared until an owning
# capability exists — any where use answers the classified
# not-implemented error before field-level semantics matter.
input OrderWhereInput {
    ids: [ID!]
}

# Saleor's order sorting input — the full pinned vocabulary verbatim.
# THREE fields execute as the real forward-only keyset sorts:
# CREATED_AT (the placement instant, id tiebreaker — with the
# deprecated CREATION_DATE alias riding the SAME executed sort,
# exactly upstream's own deprecation mapping), LAST_MODIFIED_AT (the
# entity's own audit column) and STATUS (the stored lifecycle text);
# NUMBER, RANK, CUSTOMER, PAYMENT and FULFILLMENT_STATUS answer the
# explicit not-implemented error. direction reuses the EXISTING
# shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
input OrderSortingInput {
    """Specifies the direction in which to sort orders."""
    direction: OrderDirection!

    """Sort orders by the selected field."""
    field: OrderSortField!
}

enum OrderSortField {
    """Sort orders by number (no order-number column on this platform — an explicit classified error)."""
    NUMBER

    """Sort orders by rank. Note that this option is available only with the `search` filter (search-scoped upstream — an explicit classified error)."""
    RANK

    """Sort orders by creation date (the deprecated alias of CREATED_AT — rides the SAME executed placement-instant sort)."""
    CREATION_DATE @deprecated(reason: "Use `CREATED_AT` instead.")

    """Sort orders by creation date (the placement instant)."""
    CREATED_AT

    """Sort orders by last modified date."""
    LAST_MODIFIED_AT

    """Sort orders by customer (an identity-side join this surface does not own — an explicit classified error)."""
    CUSTOMER

    """Sort orders by payment status (deprecated upstream against the legacy Payments API — an explicit classified error)."""
    PAYMENT @deprecated(reason: "The legacy Payments API is deprecated and will be removed. Use the Transactions API instead.")

    """Sort orders by fulfillment status (deprecated upstream — an explicit classified error)."""
    FULFILLMENT_STATUS @deprecated(reason: "Use `STATUS` instead.")

    """
    Sort orders by order status.

    Added in Saleor 3.22.
    """
    STATUS
}

# Saleor's order status vocabulary — declared VERBATIM (the full
# pinned enum); the platform machine's own four states render through
# it by the registered ADAPT mapping (PLACED -> UNCONFIRMED, CONFIRMED
# -> UNFULFILLED, FULFILLED -> FULFILLED, CANCELLED -> CANCELED), and
# the other five values stay inert SDL vocabulary this platform never
# emits (DRAFT/EXPIRED have no platform lifecycle counterpart;
# PARTIALLY_FULFILLED/PARTIALLY_RETURNED/RETURNED land with the
# fulfillment/returns projections' own later slices).
enum OrderStatus {
    """The order is a draft (never emitted by this platform)."""
    DRAFT

    """The order is placed but not yet confirmed (the platform's PLACED)."""
    UNCONFIRMED

    """The order is confirmed but not yet fulfilled (the platform's CONFIRMED)."""
    UNFULFILLED

    """The order is partially fulfilled (never emitted by this platform yet)."""
    PARTIALLY_FULFILLED

    """The order is partially returned (never emitted by this platform yet)."""
    PARTIALLY_RETURNED

    """The order is returned (never emitted by this platform yet)."""
    RETURNED

    """The order is fulfilled (the platform's FULFILLED)."""
    FULFILLED

    """The order is canceled (the platform's CANCELLED)."""
    CANCELED

    """The order is expired (never emitted by this platform)."""
    EXPIRED
}